WEBVTT

00:00:03.439 --> 00:00:06.940
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Monday the twenty-seventh. Have we all got sound?</v>

00:00:08.369 --> 00:00:14.320
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, sound's fine. Unlike the heating in the portakabin. It's either the Arctic or a tropical greenhouse.</v>

00:00:15.279 --> 00:00:17.730
<v Jamie Brennan>Which one have you got this morning?</v>

00:00:18.879 --> 00:00:22.379
<v Callum Reid>Greenhouse. Came in with a coat on, nearly passed out.</v>

00:00:24.609 --> 00:00:27.410
<v Sarah Okafor>Very glamorous, factory life. Right, let's get going.</v>

00:00:28.679 --> 00:00:32.880
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Hang on, am I coming through? Teams had the wrong microphone again.</v>

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:37.600
<v Fiona Doyle>You're through. Bit echoey, but we can hear you.</v>

00:00:40.079 --> 00:00:45.679
<v Marcus Hale>Before we start, I finished the repair on the old turbine last night. That's all sorted.</v>

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:47.289
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Cheers.</v>

00:00:47.759 --> 00:00:51.259
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, nice to have that one out of the way.</v>

00:00:52.159 --> 00:00:55.659
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, new stuff. What's the position with the replacement parts?</v>

00:00:56.759 --> 00:01:04.109
<v Callum Reid>I'll go to the treatment plant to pick up the replacement parts for the line one HPU today. It's fairly important.</v>

00:01:04.859 --> 00:01:07.659
<v Jamie Brennan>That's a collection, then, rather than another order?</v>

00:01:09.359 --> 00:01:11.810
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, just picking the replacement parts up.</v>

00:01:13.599 --> 00:01:15.700
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Callum Reid. Collection today, agreed.</v>

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:20.349
<v Callum Reid>Full name. Sounds like I'm in trouble.</v>

00:01:22.359 --> 00:01:25.159
<v Aisha Begum>Only when she puts the middle name in.</v>

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:28.480
<v Sarah Okafor>Don't tempt me. What else have we got?</v>

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:34.189
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah so, I'll chase the purchase order for the palletiser. I'll do that Monday.</v>

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:38.879
<v Jamie Brennan>The PO itself, yeah? Not chasing a delivery date?</v>

00:01:41.269 --> 00:01:44.420
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, the purchase order. That's what I'm chasing today.</v>

00:01:46.359 --> 00:01:48.459
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers, Haley. Monday for that, then.</v>

00:01:50.569 --> 00:01:51.769
<v Marcus Hale>Yep, got it.</v>

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:56.170
<v Callum Reid>He gets a nickname, I get the register read out.</v>

00:01:57.510 --> 00:01:58.709
<v Marcus Hale>Favouritism, obviously.</v>

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:05.879
<v Sarah Okafor>Absolutely. Right, more seriously, the near miss at the Boiler Safety Relief Valve needs writing up.</v>

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:13.750
<v Tomasz Nowak>I'll write up the near miss at the Boiler Safety Relief Valve. That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:02:14.439 --> 00:02:17.240
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, that's the one holding us. Agreed, first.</v>

00:02:18.349 --> 00:02:21.150
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Tomasz. You take the write-up, first priority.</v>

00:02:23.599 --> 00:02:25.349
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yep. I'll do that first.</v>

00:02:27.439 --> 00:02:30.939
<v Aisha Begum>Mm. Not something we want half a description of, either.</v>

00:02:31.590 --> 00:02:32.990
<v Sarah Okafor>Quite. What else, Marcus?</v>

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:39.639
<v Marcus Hale>I'll book a contractor to look at the desiccant unit by next Tuesday. No rush on that one.</v>

00:02:40.229 --> 00:02:44.430
<v Tomasz Nowak>Sorry, next Tuesday for making the booking, or for them being here?</v>

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:52.000
<v Marcus Hale>Making the booking by next Tuesday. I'm not saying they'll be on site that day.</v>

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:57.590
<v Sarah Okafor>Fine, Marcus, that's yours. No rush, booking by next Tuesday.</v>

00:02:57.979 --> 00:02:59.729
<v Marcus Hale>Yep, that's what I meant.</v>

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:04.770
<v Jamie Brennan>Fair question. Those two dates get muddled quite easily.</v>

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:12.810
<v Sarah Okafor>One more: the pressure drop on the boiler feed pump. Aisha, can you investigate that, due on Friday? Low priority.</v>

00:03:14.569 --> 00:03:18.770
<v Aisha Begum>Um, no, sorry. I haven't got the capacity to take that on.</v>

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:25.590
<v Sarah Okafor>All right. Doyler, can you take the investigation instead? Same deadline, on Friday, low priority.</v>

00:03:27.219 --> 00:03:34.219
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, I'll take it. I'll investigate the pressure drop on the boiler feed pump, due on Friday. Low priority, understood.</v>

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:39.830
<v Aisha Begum>Cheers. Better than me saying yes and sitting on it.</v>

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:43.129
<v Fiona Doyle>No, that's fine. I've got room for that.</v>

00:03:44.389 --> 00:03:46.490
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks. That goes to Doyler, then.</v>

00:03:48.439 --> 00:03:53.340
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, I talked over the end there. Nothing to add, just saying I heard.</v>

00:03:54.159 --> 00:03:58.360
<v Sarah Okafor>No worries. Everyone clear on the order? The near-miss write-up comes first.</v>

00:03:59.949 --> 00:04:01.150
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, clear.</v>

00:04:03.219 --> 00:04:06.370
<v Callum Reid>And I've got the parts collection today. All good.</v>

00:04:08.590 --> 00:04:10.689
<v Sarah Okafor>Anything we've missed before we finish?</v>

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:12.979
<v Jamie Brennan>Nothing else from stores.</v>

00:04:15.379 --> 00:04:16.579
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Nothing from me.</v>

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:18.319
<v Aisha Begum>No, I'm good.</v>

00:04:18.819 --> 00:04:20.019
<v Fiona Doyle>Same here.</v>

00:04:20.519 --> 00:04:22.620
<v Marcus Hale>All good. Enjoy the tropical portakabin.</v>

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:27.550
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, thanks, everyone. Catch you out there.</v>
